# Plan: Decision Maker App (Angular 21 + Material)

Build the task prioritization app from `app-description.md` in three layers (application / domain / infrastructure), driven by the criteria in `acceptance-criteria.md`. Domain logic stays pure and signal-based, data access goes through a port so tests can use a mock adapter. Work is grouped into 7 phases; each phase ends with green tests for its own AC block.

## Phase 1 – Setup & cleanup *(blocks everything)*

1. Install Angular Material/CDK via `ng add @angular/material` (adds theme, `provideAnimationsAsync`, roboto/icons).
2. Remove routing: delete `src/app/app.routes.ts`, drop `provideRouter` from `src/app/app.config.ts`, drop `RouterOutlet` from `src/app/app.ts` and `router-outlet` from `src/app/app.html`. Satisfies AC-10.2.
3. Rewrite `src/app/app.spec.ts` (its current `Hello, Playground` assertion will fail after step 2).
4. Create folder skeleton `src/app/domain`, `src/app/infrastructure`, `src/app/application`.
5. Define the 5 rating colors as CSS custom properties in `src/styles.scss` (`--rating-very-low` … `--rating-very-high`) plus the `rating--*` classes from AC-0.3.

## Phase 2 – Domain *(depends on 1; steps 6–8 parallel)*

6. `domain/models/task.ts`: `CriterionValue`, `Task`, `TaskDraft` (task without `id`/`createdAt`), `RatingLevel` enum — exactly as specified in AC-0.1.
7. `domain/rating.ts`: `calculateRating`, `getRatingLevel`, `criterionLabel`, `ratingLevelClass` → tests for **AC-1.x, AC-3.x**.
8. `domain/sorting.ts`: `sortByRating` (rating desc, tie-break `createdAt` asc, non-mutating) → tests for **AC-2.x**.
9. `domain/ports/task-repository.port.ts`: `TaskRepositoryPort` interface (`load()`, `save(tasks)`) + `TASK_REPOSITORY` InjectionToken. This is the port required by the *Testing* section of the description.
10. `domain/task-store.ts`: `providedIn: 'root'`, `inject(TASK_REPOSITORY)`, private `#tasks = signal<Task[]>()`, public `tasks`/`sortedTasks` as `computed()`, methods `add`, `update`, `remove`, `breakDown`, all immutable + persisting → tests for **AC-4.x** (run with the mock adapter, no `localStorage`).

## Phase 3 – Infrastructure *(depends on 9; parallel with Phase 4)*

11. `infrastructure/local-storage-task.repository.ts`: key `decision-maker.tasks`, `JSON.parse` in try/catch, per-record schema guard (`isTask`) filtering invalid entries → tests for **AC-5.1 … AC-5.5**.
12. `infrastructure/in-memory-task.repository.ts`: mock adapter implementing the same port, seedable, records `save` calls — used by all store/component tests to keep mock and real implementation in sync.
13. Provide `{ provide: TASK_REPOSITORY, useClass: LocalStorageTaskRepository }` in `src/app/app.config.ts`.

## Phase 4 – UI components *(depends on 2+6; steps 14–16 parallel with each other)*

14. `application/task-table/`: `mat-table` with columns title / expectation / time effort / work effort / rating / actions, `input()` for tasks, `output()` `breakDown`, `edit`, `delete`, `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`, row class via `[class]` binding from `ratingLevelClass`, hover handled by a `hoveredId` signal toggled through `(mouseenter)`/`(mouseleave)`/`(focusin)`/`(focusout)` in the `host`/row bindings → tests for **AC-6.x**.
15. `application/task-form-dialog/`: reactive form (`title`, three criteria), each criterion a `mat-slider` (min 0, max 5, step 1, `discrete`) with the label from `criterionLabel` shown below, live rating preview via `computed()`, confirm disabled while invalid → tests for **AC-7.x**.
16. `application/break-down-dialog/`: read-only `source-task` block, `FormArray` of sub-task rows (start with 1, add/remove, remove disabled when only one row), confirm returns `TaskDraft[]` → tests for **AC-8.x**.

## Phase 5 – Integration *(depends on 3, 4)*

17. `application/task-facade.ts`: injects `TaskStore` + `MatDialog`, exposes `tasks`, and methods `createTask()`, `editTask(id)`, `deleteTask(id)`, `breakDownTask(id)` that open dialogs and only mutate the store on a defined result.
18. `application/task-page/`: toolbar with `new-task-button`, `app-task-table` bound to `facade.tasks()`, wiring of the three outputs. Render it from `src/app/app.ts` → tests for **AC-9.x**.
19. Delete confirmation via a small `mat-dialog` confirm (AC-6.2 in the old numbering / AC-9.3 cancel path).

## Phase 6 – Cross-cutting

20. Accessibility: `aria-label` on all icon-only buttons (incl. task title), dialog focus trap check → **AC-10.5**.
21. Architecture guard: a plain unit test that reads the files under `domain/` and asserts no import path contains `application/` or `infrastructure/` → **AC-10.3**.
22. Sync `acceptance-criteria.md` with the decisions: AC-7.1/AC-7.4 rewritten for `mat-slider` (`MatSliderHarness`, clamping instead of select options), AC-6.6 rewritten to assert the `row--hovered` class toggle.

## Phase 7 – Verification

23. `npm test` — all AC-tagged suites green; check that unit suites (`[U]`) require no `TestBed`.
24. `npm run build` — production build without budget errors.
25. Manual smoke run via `npm start`: create 3 tasks with different ratings, verify order + colors, hover reveals the break-down button, break down the top task, reload the page and confirm persistence.

